{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404816-evocation-feedback-sought","id":1404816,"title":"Evocation Feedback sought","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-26T13:09:33-07:00","id":1404816,"title":"Evocation Feedback sought","content":"<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:BlackChancery\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Verdant Springwood (Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022 Jade Powerbow)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Verdant Springwood was carved during the Shogunate for the Busujima Clan, later than Ebony Fronds, for use by Shutaro\u2019s eldest son, Mamoru. Carved from a yew tree allowed to fall of age and storm, it was lacquered with the sap of a lacquer tree mixed with a small amount of green jade, then after several coats, the words \u201cthe Green gives life and takes it away\u201d painted on it in green, then more coats of lacquer. The bow, like the armour, was for a long time, used in time of war and left in the rain and sun in time of pierce. In due course, it passed into the hands of other sons, and less often daughters, of the Clan. As with their other great treasures, the Clan took great pride in knowing that they had never had to ransom it back from their enemies. After the clan\u2019s destruction, it passed into the hands of Saeko Takagi, their former retainer and recently Exalted Dawn Caste.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The bow contains a single hearthstone socket, currently empty. So long as sufficient suitable plant life is available, such as brambles, branches or vines, the attuned wielder need only set a piece to the bow for it to become an arrow, and therefore will not run out of ammunition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:BlackChancery\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Evocations of Verdant Springwood</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#01A815\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Eye of the Forest</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 3m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Resonant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Indefinite</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The wielder of Verdant Springwood is as one with the Green. This Evocation enhances Awareness rolls made while in a forest, jungle, or other vegetation-dense terrain, lowering any penalties by the wielder\u2019s (Essence).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Special activation rules</b>: As long as the wearer isn\u2019t dissonant with jade, this Evocation awakens at no cost when the bow is first is attuned and drawn in a forest, jungle, or similar.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Resonant</b>: This Evocation also reduces the benefit of plant-based cover to the wielder\u2019s targets by the wielder\u2019s (Essence).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I can't help thinking the Resonant effect is redundant, and I'm thinking to change it to &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">the benefit of plant-based cover to the wielder\u2019s targets' Stealth rolls,&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T14:24:34-07:00","id":1404832,"title":"","content":"I think that's backwards, actually-- right now, the Resonant effect helps with combat rolls, like trying to snipe an opponent who ducked behind a tree. The base effect already helps with spotting people hiding; changing the Resonant effect to penalize foes' stealth rolls just doubles down on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T15:41:00-07:00","id":1404836,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I was not at all certain of my analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key"